From: OpenATV Team <info@opena.tv>
Subject: [PATCH] libretro: honour externally supplied link flags

The makefile starts LDFLAGS from scratch, so the flags of a cross build
environment never reach the link of the core. On OpenEmbedded that drops the
distribution's hardening and optimisation options, among them -Wl,--hash-style
which the packaging QA asks for.

Setting LDFLAGS on the make command line is no way out, since the platform
blocks only append to it and the core would lose -shared and its version
script. Seed the variable from EXTRA_LDFLAGS instead, which keeps the
standalone build unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 backends/platform/libretro/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backends/platform/libretro/Makefile b/backends/platform/libretro/Makefile
--- a/backends/platform/libretro/Makefile
+++ b/backends/platform/libretro/Makefile
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
 CP       := cp
 
 
-LDFLAGS :=
+LDFLAGS := $(EXTRA_LDFLAGS)
 
 
 # Raspberry Pi 1
